<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First English Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1642–1646</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a> was fought from 1642 to 1646 between the Royalist supporters of King Charles I and the Parliamentarians. After indecisive early battles such as Edgehill, Parliament gained the upper hand at Marston Moor (1644) and, with the New Model Army, at Naseby (1645); Charles surrendered to the Scots in 1646.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-english-civil-war.jpg" alt="First English Civil War" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Barker (1811-1886) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Marston_Moor_1644_by_John_Barker.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
